  "kind": "geographic",
  "status": "current",
  "year": 1958,
  "authority": "US Board on Geographic Names (1946) and UK Permanent Committee on Geographical Names (1958); updated 2019 (checked December 2019)",
  "description": "BGN/PCGN system for Persian (Farsi) geographical names in Iran, also the basis of most English reference spellings: short vowels a e o, long ā ī ū, diphthongs ey ow, kh sh zh gh ch, homophone letters kept apart with diacritics (s̄ ş, z̄ z ẕ z̧, ţ, ḩ), ‘ for ʿayn and ’ for hamza, final silent h = -eh.",
  "sources": [
    "https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e1eeaafe5274a4f0f57553a/ROMANIZATION_OF_PERSIAN.pdf",
    "https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/romanisation-systems",
    "https://www.eki.ee/wgrs/rom1_fa.pdf"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Note 5: tashdīd doubles the letter; on ye it gives -īy- when the first ye is a vowel (Ḩoseynīyeh) and -yy- when it is a consonant (Seyyed).",
    "Note 6: ezafe -e after a consonant, -ye after a vowel or silent he (Kūh-e Marghūb, Pā-ye Āb, Dahāneh-ye Mambar). Note 8: final he after zīr is -eh, after a long vowel h.",
    "Special Rule 1: the Arabic article is Al name-initially and ol inside a name, assimilated before sun letters, lower case and written separately (Al Ḩebāl, ‘Abd or Raḩmān, Zeyn od Dīn).",
    "Special Rule 4: names ending in Allāh are one word with o (‘Abdollāh); standalone Allāh; -ābād is joined to the preceding word (Raḩmatābād). Special Rule 5: خو + ا/ی = khv (Khvājeh).",
    "Note 3: a middle dot separates k·h, z·h, s·h, g·h (not applied to a word-final silent h).",
    "ZWNJ (U+200C) is removed and the parts are joined, as Persian script does not separate them with a space (Special Rule 2).",
    "Special Rule 3 (false generics) and the Turkic suffix list of Rule 4 depend on word knowledge and are not automated."
  ],
